                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ff4a9154-8601-4a36-8d48-d6583e8b7040",
                        "source_entry_id": "4f33d539-2e10-314f-8194-e46acf36e184",
                        "source_sense_id": "a7030837-f946-33e5-8174-4b41879007a5",
                        "source_sense_description": "Göttin im Hinduismus",
                        "target_lang_word": "Kali",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kali",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2ff8bb28-490e-3017-909f-3e41c7aa873b",
                                        "entry_id": "caca9181-e597-31cf-9c30-d55c5b32f50d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A goddess in Hinduism, one of the most significant figures within that religion, who destroys evil forces and bestows liberation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Hinduism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92b86e49-1d1f-4e85-96fd-2b04a099cbfd",
                                                "sense_id": "2ff8bb28-490e-3017-909f-3e41c7aa873b",
                                                "text": "Kālī is Śiva's \"other\" wife, as it were, provoking him and encouraging him in his mad, antisocial, often disruptive habits. It is never Kālī who tames Śiva but Śiva who must becalm Kālī."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8032a38-e03f-40f7-b805-8c448190f5a4",
                                                "sense_id": "2ff8bb28-490e-3017-909f-3e41c7aa873b",
                                                "text": "To many Hindu Bengalis, Kālī is the most important divinity. Identified with the great Goddess, Devi Bhagavati, she subsumes all other goddesses."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9612d64-a1ab-4f53-8ec0-2b7006d47391",
                                                "sense_id": "2ff8bb28-490e-3017-909f-3e41c7aa873b",
                                                "text": "A popular form of Kali worshiped in Calcutta is Adya Shakti Kali, or Kali as primordial power. Adya Shakti Kali is also present in some tantras, especially the Mahanirvana Tantra. Because she devours Kala or Time, she is Kali, the original form of all things, and because she is the origin and devourer of all things, she is called Adya Kali."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "123bd2f3-bd54-3eea-b616-ac7308ed4c3c",
                                        "entry_id": "caca9181-e597-31cf-9c30-d55c5b32f50d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female given name from Sanskrit used especially in India."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kali",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "496b31ce-1988-3bd4-81b7-f72c5701edca",
                                        "entry_id": "b75eb082-5885-39c6-925d-5485f8bb39a8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male demon, lord of Kali Yuga and the nemesis of Kalki, tenth avatar of Vishnu."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Hinduism"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
